# a symlinked venv is the standard git-worktree pattern; ".venv/" with a
# trailing slash matches directories only and lets the symlink leak in.
.venv
uiproof/
.claude/launch.json

# Live-preview validation artifacts (screenshots, matrices). Never committed.
# ANCHORED to the repo root on purpose. Unanchored, `validation/` matches a
# directory at ANY depth, and it silently swallowed
# `src/intent_engine/validation/` — the canonical 100-company manifest and the
# Breaker-10 cohort selector. `git status` stayed clean, the tracked tests and
# break proofs that import it could not run from a fresh checkout of the frozen
# SHA, and for a while the only copy of that module in existence was an
# untracked file in one ephemeral scratchpad worktree.
/validation/
# Day 17 — unattended market operation. Runtime state, never source.
#
# Locks are per-process; run records and per-cycle reports are MACHINE-SPECIFIC
# operating history. Committing them would let a fresh checkout inherit another
# machine's uptime and "prove" an operational record it has not demonstrated —
# the same reasoning as data/.boot_ledger.jsonl above.
#
# NOT ignored, deliberately: reports/funnel_history.json and
# reports/market/research_assets.jsonl. Those are RESEARCH — the measurements
# and the beliefs — and they are the only thing this project actually owns.
/locks/
/status/
/dryrun/
data/dryrun/
reports/market/*_day.md
reports/market/*_day.json
reports/market/*_night.md
reports/market/*_night.json
reports/market/latest_*.json
reports/market/signal_audit.jsonl

# Day 18 — replay working state. Checkpoints and the price cache are
# machine-specific and regenerable; the RESULTS (pilot_replay.json,
# experiments.jsonl, strategies.jsonl) are research and stay tracked.
reports/market/replay/price_cache/
reports/market/replay/replay_*.json

# Runtime agent ownership markers — never committed.
.agent-lock/
